    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0048" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24260: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-15T17:00:00-04:00">September 15,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1494. For Secretary and Under Secretary. Barros Jarpa told Rockefeller<anchor
                        n="48" xml:id="d42-f1"/> today that he has just received telegram to effect
                    Secretary Hull said failure to break relations before going to States not so
                    important. We have them all punch-drunk on this issue. Please telegraph if this
                    statement was justified in Mr. Hull’s conference with Michels yesterday.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="48" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
                <p>Nelson A. Rockefeller, Coordinator of Inter-American Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
